codex
A viable route has emerged, but it is not the naïve polygon planting. I’m using the exact “Min Segment Hitting” family defined in Section 3—the NP-complete geometric source problem the paper reduces to sliding-camera guarding. The generator will compose its unit-segment gadgets with a uniquely solvable XOR construction and declare Track B: four-clause parity recognition plus GF(2) elimination is an efficient mechanical solver, while the proposed answer is a compact, exactly checked geometric line-cover certificate. I’m stress-testing whether simpler frequency, greedy, restart, and obvious-pattern attacks recover it.
